    "title": "Groundbreaking held for new playground in Albany's Washington Park - NewsBreak",
    "text": "ALBANY, N.Y. ( NEWS10 ) — Mayor Kathy Sheehan and other officials came together on Wednesday for the groundbreaking of a new playground in Albany’s Washington Park . The new playground is scheduled to open in the fall and will replace the previous playground. The mayor shared the vision of what the future park will look like. “We are going to see new equipment: a swing, spin and climb zone; a tot spot for babies and toddlers; a meadow, which is an historic feature that will be unprogrammed but open to whether it’s the library coming and doing reading or art or all kinds of opportunities for open play,” she said. The playground will remain closed during construction. In the meantime, locals can visit other playgrounds throughout the city, including: Read the latest from NEWS10: NEWS10 is the Capital Region’s local news leader! For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to NEWS10 ABC.",
